        },
        "long_description": {
          "before": "Lingo.dev is a localization engineering platform where teams create localization engines – stateful translation APIs configured with glossaries, brand voice rules, per-locale model preferences, and quality scoring. Each engine persists domain context across every request via retrieval augmented localization (RAL). Integrate via API, CLI, CI/CD, or other integrations. Localization infrastructure behind 200M+ translated words for teams including Mistral, Solana, SoSafe, and Cal.com.",
          "after": "Lingo.dev is the localization engineering platform: the best way to measure translation quality, translate with LLMs, and proofread with native speakers.\r\n\r\nLingo.dev is built for teams accountable for quality in languages they can't read. Teams configure localization engines, stateful translation APIs that hold the glossary, brand voice, and per-locale model preferences, and every request retrieves that context at inference time through retrieval augmented localization. Every translation is scored before it goes live, scores and corrections tune the engine, and the localization team runs the localization infrastructure. Integrate through the API, CLI, CI/CD, or native integrations with the code repository and the CMS. \r\n\r\nLingo.dev is the standard localization infrastructure for modern enterprise teams scaling into new markets – including Mistral, Solana, SoSafe, and Cal.com. Over 300M words processed, SOC 2 Type II compliant."
        },
